one with Drive,

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:33.060
which will hit 8 billion
users, active users monthly,

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:33.900
going forward.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:37.980
The key here is big
data is in our DNA.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:39.090
We leverage data.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:41.430
We leverage machine
learning for giving those

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:44.430
amazing experiences in
all of these products.

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:47.220
And the way we do that is
through internal technology

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:50.460
that we have built. If you
think about Dremel, which

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.630
we use internally for
all our analytics,

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.230
BigQuery is actually
an enterprise version

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:57.270
of that same piece
of technology that's

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:58.830
available for enterprises.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:01.200
So what we are doing here
is bringing the technology

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.600
that we have invested
over years and making

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.530
it available for our
customers in the Cloud.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:11.730
If you think about it, data
across the world is growing.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.820
It will be 163
zettabytes by 2025.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.970
And as datasets grow
within organizations,

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.400
you want to have infrastructure.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.800
You want to have analytics
capability that can actually

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.320
process that amount of data.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.460
Just a data point--
one of our customers

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:31.380
really, when they
started their data

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.470
collection and their
streaming analytics biplanes,

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:36.960
they used to collect like
50 million events a day.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.790
Now they are up to five
billion within 18 months.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:43.380
So what happens is, as you start
seeing value from your data,

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:44.930
you will collect more and more.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.800
But you want ability
and infrastructure

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.190
that can actually seamlessly
scale as your needs grow

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:51.900
within your organizations.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.880
Similarly, there
was a survey done--

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:57.480
MIT survey was done about
machine learning and AI,

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.060
how many customers are
using it, how it was going.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:03.030
The key thing was
the organizations

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:07.440
that are actually using AI
are able to make 2x faster

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:10.220
decisions, 5x faster decisions.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:13.710
They're able to do two times
more data-driven decisions

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.450
within their
organizations, and also

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:19.320
3x faster execution on the
decisions that they are making.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:22.100
So overall, if you think
about it, machine learning,

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:25.060
AI is going to be critical
for all your organizations.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:27.450
And then the key
point though is,

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:30.180
if your organization is
not good at analytics,

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.980
it's never going
to be great at AI.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.080
So the first thing,
the foundation--

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.650
you have to have great
foundation on analytics data.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:37.650
How do you process data?

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.775
How do you analyze data?

00:03:38.775 --> 00:03:40.650
And then you can think
about how you go ahead

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:43.090
and do machine learning on
top of that data, leverage

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:45.840
AI for differentiation.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:49.620
If you look at the numbers,
though, less than 1%

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.560
of world's unstructured
data is actually

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.920
being used for analytics
and analysis today.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.700
Less than 50% of structured
data is analyzed today

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.510
within organizations.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:03.390
So what is our approach to this?

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:05.820
If you look at Google,
what are we doing?

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:07.000
There are four key things.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:11.850
One, we are focusing on
infrastructure or solutions

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:15.150
that allow you to go out
and focus on analytics, not

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:15.940
infrastructure.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.730
We'll talk more about that.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:20.220
The second is developing
comprehensive solutions.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:24.000
So we know customers need the
whole portfolio of solutions

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.510
to go ahead and do analysis.

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:27.630
We are focusing on
end-to-end, all the components

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:28.720
that you need.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:32.470
End-to-end ML lifecycle, and
we'll look at that quickly.

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:34.050
And then innovative and open--

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:36.420
being an open cloud,
making sure you

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.120
have options with
open source software

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:42.090
so that you can go ahead and
run the workloads the way you

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:44.190
want to run is super
critical for us.

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:46.350
And we have lot of
investments that we do

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:49.470
in making sure we promote that.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:52.800
Let's talk about what does
focusing on analytic means

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.210
and not on infrastructure.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:56.340
If you think about us--
if you're doing analysis

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:58.860
with BigQuery, which
is our cloud scale

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:03.150
[INAUDIBLE] product, you can
get started within seconds.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:05.400
You basically can
bring your datasets

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.710
and start analyzing instantly.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:11.310
The key thing is, if you're
not using a serverless product

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.662
like BigQuery or
Dataflow, you will

00:05:13.662 --> 00:05:15.120
have to worry about
monitoring, you

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:16.620
will have to worry
about performance

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.690
tuning, infrastructure.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:20.380
How many nodes do I need?

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.910
What kind of cluster
size do I need?

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:23.370
How do you performance tune?

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:25.590
None of that is going to
be a problem if you're

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:26.550
focused on serverless.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:27.801
So that's what our focus is.

00:05:27.801 --> 00:05:29.550
We want to provide you
with infrastructure

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.839
that automatically scales, gives
you ability to do analysis,

00:05:32.839 --> 00:05:34.630
and you don't have to
worry about anything.

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:38.490
Just bring your data,
start doing analysis on it.

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:40.380
Let's talk about
the second point--

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:42.720
end-to-end
comprehensive solutions.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:46.860
The big thing is, if you
think about analysis,

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.930
it actually starts
with ingestion.

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:50.400
How do I get my data?

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.280
The first step is, how do
I get my streaming data?

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:56.910
We have lots of customers using
massive amount of streaming

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.010
events that are coming to them.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:01.440
And how do you scale this
infrastructure seamlessly?

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.210
So Cloud Pub/Sub is
our solution that

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:06.120
allows you to do millions
of events per second

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:09.420
that you can collect
and do analysis on them.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.850
Similarly, a lot
of our customers

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:15.050
use different Google
products, like, for example,

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:18.240
AdWords and DoubleClick
and all of those,

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:19.710
for advertising purposes.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:22.725
What we have done is we've made
it really easy for customers

00:06:22.725 --> 00:06:26.377
who want to use Google Cloud
for marketing analytics.

00:06:26.377 --> 00:06:27.960
Within a few clicks,
you can literally

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:30.870
go ahead and get your AdWords
data, your DoubleClick data,

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:34.560
into BigQuery for
analysis seamlessly.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.774
Similarly, IoT is
super critical.

00:06:36.774 --> 00:06:38.940
You saw some amazing
announcements yesterday morning

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:43.050
with HTPU and on Cloud IoT core.

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:44.340
We have a Cloud IoT course.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:46.360
If you are interested
in collecting IoT data,

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:48.430
you can seamlessly
collect that and actually

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:50.500
leverage the whole
platform from there.

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:52.290
So we've covered the ingestion.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:54.870
If you think about reliable
data processing and streaming

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:57.900
pipelines, we have multiple
options for our customers.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:00.780
One is data flow with Beam.

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:03.810
So Beam is an open
source SDK for you

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:06.680
to build batch and
streaming pipelines

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:08.994
with the same programming model.

00:07:08.994 --> 00:07:10.410
You can use Dataflow,
which allows

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:13.410
you to automatically build
large scale data processing

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:14.460
pipelines.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:16.390
Great for developers.

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:18.540
But we also realize that
a lot of our customers

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:22.110
have in-house capabilities
with Spark and Hadoop.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:23.550
And they love Spark.

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:26.010
I used to use Spark before
in my previous role.

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:27.000
So I love Spark too.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.210
So for that, we have managed
Hadoop and Spark environment

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:31.530
with Datablock.

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:34.470
And then for
analysts-- and we know

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:37.920
a lot of our analyst community,
which is familiar with data,

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:39.600
also wants to do
raw data wrangling,

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.580
also wants to do
data preparation,

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:44.340
so that they know best
before the data is

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:46.740
used what kind of
analysis they want

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:48.340
to do and clean up the data.

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:52.420
So we have Cloud Dataprep
for those audience.

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:54.130
After that, once
your data is ready,

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:55.600
you want to do
analysis at scale.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.070
You want to build
your data lakes.

00:07:57.070 --> 00:08:00.130
You can actually use GCS,
Google Cloud Storage,

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:03.160
to go ahead and put all your
structured, unstructured data,

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:04.430
and then process it.

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:07.630
Or you can use Cloud Scale
Data Warehouse with BigQuery

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:09.580
to put all this data
at petabyte scale,

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:12.170
and then do analysis
on top of it.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:15.490
And once you have analysis
platform ready for you, then

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:18.250
for advanced analytics,
you can use ML Engine,

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:20.740
you can use TensorFlow.

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:23.020
For visualizations, you
can use Data Studio.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:25.350
We'll see some of the
new enhancements we

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:27.460
are making available on that.

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:30.190
And also Sheets, a lot of
our customers, especially

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.867
G Suite customers who
use Sheets every day--

00:08:32.867 --> 00:08:34.450
we're making some
enhancements on that

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:37.780
to easily make data from
BigQuery and other places

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:40.594
available today.

00:08:40.594 --> 00:08:41.260
So that's there.

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:43.049
If you think about
ML lifecycle--

00:08:43.049 --> 00:08:44.840
there's the whole
lifecycle, right?

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:47.300
ML lifecycle is you
start from ingestion.

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:48.400
You have to explore.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:49.940
You have to prepare.

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:51.370
You have to pre-process.

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:55.324
Then you start the process of
training, hypertuning, testing,

00:08:55.324 --> 00:08:55.990
and predictions.

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:58.150
There's a whole lifecycle
that has to happen.

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:00.280
And what we provide
is a whole suite

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:01.990
of products that
allow you to go do

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:04.700
every one of those processes.

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:07.570
But what we are also doing
is making it very easy

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:09.125
for you to do machine learning.

00:09:09.125 --> 00:09:10.750
And you heard some
of the announcements

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.040
we did earlier today.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:14.860
And I will go a bit
more detail into that.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.960
And actually, we have
an amazing demo for you

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:20.260
later in the session.

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:23.150
From a customer
momentum perspective,

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:24.100
that's our portfolio.

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:26.890
We are seeing tremendous
growth in the data analytics

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:28.330
side with our customers.

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:31.480
A lot of customers using the
whole portfolio across industry

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.760
verticals, from
financial services

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.880
to retail, from gaming
to media entertainment,

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.022
all across the
board, manufacturing.

00:09:39.022 --> 00:09:41.230
All across the board, we
are seeing tremendous growth

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:44.350
in our data analytics
capability being used

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:45.970
in different organizations.

00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:49.510
And its across the different
sizes of data sets, too.

00:09:49.510 --> 00:09:51.770
So you heard earlier
today, [INAUDIBLE]

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:54.880
