getting data from all

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.950
over, from various systems,
or so forth, basically.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:49.820
So we have data coming
from our booking system.

00:12:49.820 --> 00:12:53.240
80% of our booking goes
through our internet

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:55.760
and our mobile app,
unlike other airlines,

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:57.630
which is the other way around.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.660
And then we have data
coming from our aircraft

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:01.100
and from our engines.

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:05.660
And we use our aircraft
in the most efficient--

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:09.140
and we maximize the
utilization rate.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:12.230
The 8020 that we use,
we fly 14 hours a day.

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:14.780
And we have 25 minutes to turn
around, so that we can fit in

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:17.040
as many sectors as we can.

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:18.440
So if you look at
the whole group

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:23.960
as about departing flights,
there's about 1,500 per day.

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:26.851
And we're looking at departing
passengers about almost 300,000

00:13:26.851 --> 00:13:27.350
per day.

00:13:27.350 --> 00:13:29.000
So that's a lot of
data coming there.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.160
And it's really
important when you

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:33.140
