00:18:09.910 --> 00:18:11.345
So that's super critical.

00:18:11.345 --> 00:18:13.470
So one of the announcements
you heard today morning

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:16.320
was Rajen talking
about BigQuery ML.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:18.390
The key thing in this was--

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:20.130
the two big challenges
we started hearing

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:22.330
from our customers
was, it's great to use

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:25.499
BigQuery-- massive amount of
data, bring all the data in.

00:18:25.499 --> 00:18:27.290
But if you want to do
any machine learning,

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.140
you have to move that data out.

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:31.440
And then, if you have
seen some numbers,

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:35.460
like 80% of data scientists
spend time in data preparation,

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:39.030
moving data around, and doing
testing of the models and all,

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:41.760
so our thing was, how
do you reduce that time

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:43.260
by making machine
learning available

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:45.926
in the data warehouse and stuff,
moving data to machine learning

00:18:45.926 --> 00:18:46.560
engine?

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:49.390
Why can't I move machine
learning engine closer to data?

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:51.150
So that was the whole
premise of that.

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:53.790
The second thing
was skill set gap.

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:57.010
In the industry, we just
don't have that many PSG data

00:18:57.010 --> 00:18:59.430
scientists to go do
advanced machine learning.

00:18:59.430 --> 00:19:01.890
So our thing was,
can we just leverage

00:19:01.890 --> 00:19:05.370
the skill our audience
already has, which is SQL,

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:08.100
and then make machine learning
available to them in SQL?

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:10.840
So that's exactly what
we have tried to do.

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:16.410
BigQuery ML is nothing but
a SQL-based machine learning

00:19:16.410 --> 00:19:18.630
model creation within BigQuery.

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:20.430
If you have BigQuery,
you are already

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:22.080
using SQL to analyze data.

00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:23.400
You have queries ready.

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:24.870
You understand your data.

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:27.540
Just write two lines
of code on top of it.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:30.190
Create model, what
type of model you want.

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:32.109
We can auto-detect
models if you want.

00:19:32.109 --> 00:19:34.650
And then just give us the input
and what you want to predict.

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:38.760
And for prediction, you're
just saying, select ML.Predict,

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:40.660
and you can get the
predictions out.

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:44.250
So that's how easy
it is to do machine

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:46.650
learning within BigQuery.

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:49.110
One of the things, if
you saw earlier today,

00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:51.660
