00:27:17.260 --> 00:27:19.540
you have linear and logistic
regression models that

00:27:19.540 --> 00:27:21.010
are already available.

00:27:21.010 --> 00:27:23.710
The beta is available,
so please go try it.

00:27:23.710 --> 00:27:26.929
Give us some more
feedback in the beta mode.

00:27:26.929 --> 00:27:27.970
A couple of other things.

00:27:27.970 --> 00:27:31.010
We are also announcing
Clustering beta is coming.

00:27:31.010 --> 00:27:32.950
Again, I won't be
able to go in details

00:27:32.950 --> 00:27:35.470
of partitioning, clustering,
key capabilities.

00:27:35.470 --> 00:27:37.070
Just think about it this way--

00:27:37.070 --> 00:27:39.190
you can do a petabyte-scale
query from BigQuery.

00:27:39.190 --> 00:27:40.710
You could do it
like two years back.

00:27:40.710 --> 00:27:41.710
You can do it now.

00:27:41.710 --> 00:27:44.450
But with partitioning
plus clustering,

00:27:44.450 --> 00:27:46.760
you can reduce the
cost drastically

00:27:46.760 --> 00:27:50.150
because the queries are going
to be way more efficient.

00:27:50.150 --> 00:27:53.180
We only access the data, what
is required within that cluster

00:27:53.180 --> 00:27:54.470
or within that partition.

00:27:54.470 --> 00:27:55.930
So partitioning
plus clustering is

00:27:55.930 --> 00:27:58.750
going to help you make your
queries way more efficient

00:27:58.750 --> 00:28:00.610
and actually reduce
costs drastically

00:28:00.610 --> 00:28:02.950
if you are using
on-demand pricing model.

00:28:02.950 --> 00:28:06.874
There's a detailed session at
3:15 by Jordan Tigani today.

00:28:06.874 --> 00:28:08.290
You should absolutely
go if you're

00:28:08.290 --> 00:28:11.385
