00:46:25.236 --> 00:46:27.410
- My name is Robert Tabz.

00:46:27.410 --> 00:46:30.810
And five and a half years ago,
my mother was diagnosed with

00:46:30.810 --> 00:46:31.770
Alzheimer's.

00:46:31.770 --> 00:46:33.960
I knew not all the
medicines were working.

00:46:33.960 --> 00:46:37.185
The entire time was
a downward spiral.

00:46:37.185 --> 00:46:40.160
- I also lost my grandfather
about 25 years ago

00:46:40.160 --> 00:46:41.250
to the disease.

00:46:41.250 --> 00:46:44.220
My family, at the time,
felt like it was already

00:46:44.220 --> 00:46:47.300
too late to change the
trajectory of the disease.

00:46:47.300 --> 00:46:51.480
And it breaks my heart when I
hear the same stories today.

00:46:51.480 --> 00:46:53.760
The mission for Foundation
For Precision Medicine

00:46:53.760 --> 00:46:56.010
is to bring AI and
health care together

00:46:56.010 --> 00:46:58.560
to detect Alzheimer's early.

00:46:58.560 --> 00:47:01.650
- If you can detect
Alzheimer's very early on,

00:47:01.650 --> 00:47:06.146
that is when the disease is
most susceptible to treatment.

00:47:06.146 --> 00:47:07.860
- The data that
we have access to

00:47:07.860 --> 00:47:10.710
are anonymized electronic
health care records.

00:47:10.710 --> 00:47:13.320
We needed a HIPAA-compliant
environment, which

00:47:13.320 --> 00:47:15.870
is why we used Google Cloud.

00:47:15.870 --> 00:47:18.070
- We're dealing with
hundreds of variables

00:47:18.070 --> 00:47:20.610
on millions of
patients, which generate

00:47:20.610 --> 00:47:23.515
billions of lines of data.

00:47:23.515 --> 00:47:26.790
- Google Cloud enables us
to scale our operations.

00:47:26.790 --> 00:47:29.670
And with BigQuery ML, we're
able to develop machine learning

00:47:29.670 --> 00:47:33.596
models faster and
utilize our entire data.

00:47:33.596 --> 00:47:37.710
Being a nonprofit, we rely on
our volunteers across the US,

00:47:37.710 --> 00:47:41.020
and Google Cloud really
enabled us to do that.

00:47:41.020 --> 00:47:43.890
We wanted them to be able
to apply machine learning

00:47:43.890 --> 00:47:46.800
on the data and look
at trends themselves,

00:47:46.800 --> 00:47:50.460
to empower them to come up
with more innovative approaches

00:47:50.460 --> 00:47:53.165
to change the progression
of the disease.

00:47:53.165 --> 00:47:55.060
- This work is so
important to me,

00:47:55.060 --> 00:47:58.320
because it helps us address
this devastating illness that

00:47:58.320 --> 00:48:00.180
has no cure.

00:48:00.180 --> 00:48:02.280
- I heard somewhere
that they said,

00:48:02.280 --> 00:48:06.090
don't forget the dots
on the plot are people.

00:48:06.090 --> 00:48:09.026
And we really take
that seriously.

